I'd be interested in hearing that myself.  I'd also like to hear how
long it took one of these players to finally win.

One of the things about Nethack that's simultaneously very interesting
and very frustrating is that, from the perspective of the unspoiled
player, the means of reaching the game's final goal is very difficult
to figure out.

There are a few pieces of information that are essential for winning
the game that are only revealed in major Oracle consultations, which
are not cheap for a newbie player.  That's bad enough, but an unspoiled
player also has no clue that he needs to keep buying them until he gets
the right ones.  I think it might be helpful to newbies to say
something about this in the Guidebook....

Then, there's the things that can only be learned through trial and
painful error, like the necessity of gaining magic resistance.  That
was one that I learned the hard way myself, having actually fallen
victim to the Wizard of Yendor's touch of death attack in one of the
games leading up to my first ascension.

This is one of the reasons that Nethack has a reputation for being a
player killer.  That's not necessarily a bad thing (it makes us
ascended players seem like gods to unclued folk), but it does mean,
essentially, either seek out spoilers or be prepared to play months of
years before you even have a chance at winning.


